{"id":"PLCY100","title":"Foundations of Public Policy","department":"Public Policy","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"A survey course, focusing on public policy institutions and analytical issues as well as on overview of key public policy problems. Students will be introduced to public policy as a discipline, with a brief overview of the actors and institutions involved in the process, and familiarize themselves with the kinds of problems typically requiring public action. The course will examine these problems from a multijurisdictional and multisectoral perspective. Specific policy areas examined include education policy, health policy, economic and budgetary policy, criminal justice policy, environmental policy, and national and homeland security policy. The course should permit students to have broad foundational exposure to the field that will give them a solid base for more advanced courses.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201808","sections":7,"seats":190,"openSeats":7,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Philip Joyce","M Apolonia Calderon"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":7,"seats":196,"openSeats":36,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Philip Joyce","M Apolonia Calderon"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":4,"seats":110,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Eric Luedtke","Erica Smith"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":7,"seats":196,"openSeats":13,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["M Apolonia Calderon"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":4,"seats":150,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Erica Smith","Devin Entrikin"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":7,"seats":200,"openSeats":7,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Eric Luedtke"],"removed":false},{"term":"202201","sections":5,"seats":150,"openSeats":28,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Shanna Pearson-Merkowitz"],"removed":false},{"term":"202205","sections":1,"seats":25,"openSeats":23,"wai